-# Patent Research, Drafting & Editing
-
-> An integrated workspace + toolchain for patent **prior-art search / novelty self-check / search evidence chain / drafting assistance**.
-> Three deliverables: the **skill package** (for AI clients), the **`patentkit` core** (pip package), and the **workspace data** (private, local).
-
-**Current versions**: skill package [`skill-v2.3.0`](https://github.com/cyy1018abc-kyy/Patent-Research-and-Drafting-and-Editing-/releases/tag/skill-v2.3.0) ·
-core [`patentkit-v0.1.1`](https://github.com/cyy1018abc-kyy/Patent-Research-and-Drafting-and-Editing-/releases/tag/patentkit-v0.1.1)
-(see [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) for changes)
-
-## Quick start (pick the row for your role)
-
-| I want to… | Start here |
-|---|---|
-| **Use the skill for patent research / self-checks** (Claude Code / Codex CLI / Codex desktop) | Download the [skill package release](https://github.com/cyy1018abc-kyy/Patent-Research-and-Drafting-and-Editing-/releases/tag/skill-v2.3.0) → install per [`patent-research-skill/README.md`](patent-research-skill/README.md) |
-| **Develop / extend the core** | `pip install -e ".[mcp,dev]"` → `python -m pytest` → [`patentkit/`](patentkit/) |
-| **Work in this workspace** (search / comparison / gates / delivery) | `cd` to the repo root (where `workspace.yml` lives) → follow [`docs/operations_manual.md`](docs/operations_manual.md) |
-| **Do client adaptation / cut releases** | [`release/README.md`](release/README.md), [`cross_client_tests/README.md`](cross_client_tests/README.md) |
-
-> The workspace is located by **walking up from the current directory** to find `workspace.yml`; run it elsewhere and it reports "workspace not found".
-> To use it from any directory: `$env:PATENTKIT_WORKSPACE = "<repo-root>"` (or specify `--root` for a single run).
-
-## Repository layout
-
-```
-├── README.md                 This file: entry point / quick start / layout
-├── CHANGELOG.md              Version changes for both release artifacts (skill package / core)
-├── workspace.yml             ★ Workspace marker (read by `patentkit` to locate the workspace)
-├── INDEX.md                  Workspace content index (generated by patentkit index --write)
-├── pyproject.toml            ★ pip package definition (patentkit)
-├── patentkit/                ★ Core: validation / gates / ingest / reports / MCP adapter
-├── patent-research-skill/    ★ Independently distributed skill package (SKILL.md + references + scripts + assets)
-├── release/                  Release sources (install scripts + release notes under notes/) and release process
-├── tools/                    Build / snapshot / release helper scripts
-├── tests/                    Rule regression tests (pytest; all green is the bar)
-├── docs/                     ★ Project documentation
-│   ├── operations_manual.md           From zero to delivery (commands + checkpoints + troubleshooting)
-│   ├── roadmap.md             Current roadmap: Skill-first P0–P4 (MCP frozen)
-│   ├── delivery_summary.md           Evidence-chain snapshot (generated by tools/snapshot.py)
-│   ├── release_gates_todo.md      Release gate tracking (✅ closed)
-│   ├── upgrade_plan.md         Historical baseline: 2026-10-15 diagnosis and implementation record
-│   ├── plugin_plan.md         Client-adaptation architecture analysis (roadmap section superseded)
-│   ├── public_repo_assessment.md       Risks, options, and checklist for going public (read this first)
-│   └── tool_benchmarks/             Research notes including security scanning (SkillSpector)
-├── cross_client_tests/             P3 test assets (cases/runner/validator/evidence)
-├── 00_methodology/ ~ 08_polishing/     Workspace data (search plan/logs/candidates/comparison/conclusions/drafting/polishing)
-└── .github/                  CI (install this package + full pytest + validate)
-```
-
-> `00–08` is **workspace data** (includes derived content from unpublished applications), kept separate from the code / skill package;
-> the backend data boundary is described under "Confidentiality boundary review" below.
-
-## Common commands
-
-```powershell
-pip install -e ".[mcp,dev]"        # editable install of the core + dev dependencies
-python -m pytest                    # rule regression tests
-python -m patentkit check           # CI entry point: validate + gates
-python -m patentkit status          # everything at a glance: targets/gates/validation/candidates/next steps
-python -m patentkit validate --strict
-python -m patentkit gates
-
-python tools/snapshot.py --write    # refresh docs/delivery_summary.md
-python tools/build_skill_release.py # build the skill package zip (dist/)
-```
-
-For the full command set (search, ingest, review, citations, delivery) see [`docs/operations_manual.md`](docs/operations_manual.md).
-
-## Version and count conventions (authoritative sources)
-
-> A given number may have exactly one authoritative source; other documents **reference** it instead of restating it.
-
-| Convention | Authoritative source | How other documents cite it |
-|---|---|---|
-| Core version | `__version__` in `patentkit/__init__.py`; `pyproject.toml` reads it via `dynamic = ["version"]` | Don't restate the version number |
-| Skill package version | `metadata.version` in `patent-research-skill/SKILL.md` | Reference it; don't define another |
-| MCP tool list | Registry in `patentkit/mcp_server.py` (currently **12 tools**) | Count/names must match the code (locked by `tests/test_docs.py`) |
-| Test count | `python -m pytest --collect-only -q` | **Don't hard-code a specific number** |
-| Historical baseline | [`docs/upgrade_plan.md`](docs/upgrade_plan.md) | Read as history, not as current state |
-| Current roadmap | [`docs/roadmap.md`](docs/roadmap.md) | — |
-| Auto snapshot | [`docs/delivery_summary.md`](docs/delivery_summary.md), generated by `python tools/snapshot.py --write` | A snapshot, not authoritative output |
-
-## Optional MCP adapter (P4 future option, frozen)
-
-`patentkit` is also an MCP server (`patentkit mcp`, stdio), exposing
-`patent_status` / `patent_doctor` / `patent_validate` / `patent_gates` /
-`patent_search_plan` / `patent_candidates` / `patent_references` / `patent_ingest` /
-`patent_bibsync` / `patent_attest` / `patent_fetch_cnipa` / `patent_fetch_cnipa_batch`
-— **12 tools** in total — plus methodology-document resources and preset prompts.
-
-> **Frozen**: no new tools, no scheduling; bug fixes only. Unfreezing conditions: [`docs/roadmap.md`](docs/roadmap.md) §4.5.
-> Chat-only clients (no tools) cannot use MCP; their conclusions can only reach `asserted` and must be labeled "⚠️ Unverified by tool checks".
-> For the architecture analysis see [`docs/plugin_plan.md`](docs/plugin_plan.md); the current direction is **Skill-first**.
-
-## Skill package (primary usage path)
-
-[`patent-research-skill/`](patent-research-skill/) is an independently distributable Agent Skill:
-`SKILL.md` (when to trigger / execution order / hard constraints / result format) + `references/` (6 methodology documents, loaded on demand)
-+ `scripts/` (thin wrappers for status/validate/gates/report/check) + `assets/` + `agents/openai.yaml` (desktop metadata).
-It **contains no real project data** and can be distributed externally.
-
-- **Public distribution repo (skill package source + Releases)**: <https://github.com/cyy1018abc-kyy/patent-research-skill>
-
-- Install/upgrade/compatibility matrix: [`patent-research-skill/README.md`](patent-research-skill/README.md)
-- Release package build and GitHub Release process: [`release/README.md`](release/README.md)
-- Cross-client testing (Claude Code 13/13, Codex CLI 13/13; desktop spot-checks usable):
-  [`cross_client_tests/README.md`](cross_client_tests/README.md)
-
-## Confidentiality boundary review (2026-10-21)
-
-**Conclusion: the repository must stay private; external distribution covers only code and the skill package.**
-**Review premise: GitHub repository visibility = Private (user-confirmed, 2026-10-21).**
-
-| Level | Scope | Notes |
-|---|---|---|
-| ✅ **Already public** | `07_granted_patents/` (public-status registry only) | Both patents have been granted and published; the full texts have been moved out of the repository, leaving only the registry table and sha256 |
-| ⚠️ **Internal · includes derived content from unpublished applications** | `00_methodology/`, `01_search_plan/`, `04_comparative_analysis/`, `05_novelty_conclusions/`, `07_drafting/`, `08_polishing/`, `docs/delivery_summary.md`, `workspace.yml` | TGT-0001 is not yet published; its title, technical main axes, feature-level summaries, parameters and conclusions all live here. Full texts are outside this repo |
-| ✅ **Directly distributable** | `patentkit/`, `patent-research-skill/`, `release/`, `tools/` | Code and skill package contain no project data |
-
-**Must comply**
-
-1. Do not make the repository public; do not package the whole repository for external distribution (archives / network drives / cloud-sync folders all count as external distribution).
-2. Do not upload `00–08` or `docs/delivery_summary.md` to cloud AI clients; `patentkit/` and `patent-research-skill/` are fine.
-3. Distribute only the skill package and `patentkit/` externally; keep workspace data on the local machine.
-4. Before delivery / external distribution, tick off each item in the "Pre-delivery/public-disclosure · confidentiality checklist" in [`docs/operations_manual.md`](docs/operations_manual.md).
-
-## Language policy
-
-- The **documentation, code, tests, configuration and the skill package are written in English.**
-- **Workspace data is archived in its original language (Chinese) and is intentionally not translated**:
-  search-log evidence (`02_search_logs/`), candidate records (`03_candidates/`), review worksheets
