+## Version and count conventions (authoritative sources)
+
+> A given number may have exactly one authoritative source; other documents **reference** it instead of restating it.
+
+| Convention | Authoritative source | How other documents cite it |
+|---|---|---|
+| Core version | `__version__` in `patentkit/__init__.py`; `pyproject.toml` reads it via `dynamic = ["version"]` | Don't restate the version number |
+| Skill package version | `metadata.version` in `patent-research-skill/SKILL.md` | Reference it; don't define another |
+| MCP tool list | Registry in `patentkit/mcp_server.py` (currently **12 tools**) | Count/names must match the code (locked by `tests/test_docs.py`) |
+| Test count | `python -m pytest --collect-only -q` | **Don't hard-code a specific number** |
+| Historical baseline | [`docs/upgrade_plan.md`](docs/upgrade_plan.md) | Read as history, not as current state |
+| Current roadmap | [`docs/roadmap.md`](docs/roadmap.md) | — |
+| Auto snapshot | [`docs/delivery_summary.md`](docs/delivery_summary.md), generated by `python tools/snapshot.py --write` | A snapshot, not authoritative output |
